).</blockquote><div class=3D"theme-doc-markdown markdown"><header><h1>Compi=
le-time evaluation</h1></header><p>To understand Mojo's metaprogramming, yo=
u need to understand how Mojo runs
code at compile time. Several things can trigger compile-time code executio=
n:</p>
<ul>
<li class=3D"">Assigning an expression to a <code>comptime</code> value.</l=
i>
<li class=3D"">Evaluating a <code>comptime</code> conditional or loop.</li>
<li class=3D"">Assigning an expression to a compile-time parameter.</li>
<li class=3D"">And a few less common cases, all identified with the <code>c=
omptime</code> keyword.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here are some examples:</p>
